title five of six aloft -- Dream joins, and every repair of the last day is proven in one chain
prompt Keaton pasted Dream's clean launch: the flake switch against grain-dream, both binaries verified in the new store path, a warning-free pong, the round-open adopting the anointed order, and the loop running.
think The chain that put Dream up proved every layer this day built, in order. The flake switch pointed at grain-dream's checkout carried the overlay because the round-open had already adopted cb80e26a16 there; readlink showed a NEW store hash with codex-code-mode-host beside codex; the pong came back with the warning line GONE, which is the reading that matters, since a bare pong exercises no tool call and only the absent warning proves the host resolves; and the next round-open printed behind -- adopted the anointed order, the self-healing open's first production adopt on the pier, picking up c83e0ca25 without a hand.
think The rebuild misfire had its own lesson worth keeping: rebuild-outer.sh reads /home/keeper/grain/nixos -- Hush's checkout -- and at rebuild time that tree had not pulled the overlay commit, so the first rebuild faithfully rebuilt the elder config. The one-off flake switch against grain-dream was the safe path precisely because a manual round-open in Hush's live checkout would have stashed a running lap's work out from under it. A rebuild reads a checkout, and which checkout is part of the instruction.
obs Five of six bodies live: Mind on its new bounded loop, Silence on this Mac mid-lap with the ledger staged, Hush on the pier, Dream now in its own clone grain-dream, Sound at this bench. Mystery alone waits on the Framework. The fullest hour the fleet has had.
obs The ledger row for my fail-closed interim still waits -- Silence's lap holds REDS mid-fold, and the derive scan reads next=312, so a sibling booked %311 upstream while this bench worked. The row books at the next free number when the pin frees; the commit body of c83e0ca25 carries the account meanwhile.
